  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2024) position from Midland Bank's own audited annual report \"MDB Financial Performance and Ratios: 5 Years Overview\", taken from the FY2024 report (the reporting year's own document). SOLO / STANDALONE basis. Midland Bank was licensed in 2013, so FY2013 is the bank's first year of operation and this series covers its entire public history; there is no FY2011 or FY2012 to report. All figures are as reported by the bank; the source table prints total liabilities directly, so nothing on the balance sheet is derived. The row mapped to operating_profit is the bank's 'Profit before provision and tax' (labelled 'Profit before provision on loans and corporate tax' in some years), i.e. pre-provision operating profit. RESTATEMENTS -- 3 figure(s) here are reported differently by other Midland Bank annual reports; the contemporaneous value is kept and the divergence recorded: foreign_remittance: this record uses 14327 (AR2024); AR2025 report 9594; nav_per_share: this record uses 15.13 (AR2024); AR2025 report 14.69; cost_of_fund_pct: this record uses 9.51 (AR2024); AR2025 report 7.18. Classified loans are calculated as the reported NPL percentage applied to reported loans and advances, because the source table prints the ratio but not the absolute figure for most years. The provision charge for the year is calculated as profit before provision and tax minus profit after provision before tax; the source table's own provision row wraps across two lines and its label is lost in text extraction in several reports. The derivation reproduces the printed figure exactly where it is readable (FY2025: 2,702 - 1,110 = 1,592; FY2024: 2,114 - 1,125 = 989; FY2023: 1,743 - 1,277 = 466).",
